<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jones–Shafroth Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jones Act of 1917</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jones–Shafroth Act was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> law of 1917 that granted United States citizenship to the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>. It also reorganised the island's government, creating an elected Senate and a bill of rights, while the governor and other high officials were still appointed from Washington. It remained Puerto Rico's basic law until the Commonwealth constitution of 1952.</p></div>
